
Implement only SUITE-level XML parameter loading
in the existing TestNG lifecycle adapter.

The framework parameter layer loader already
exists but is not connected to production lifecycle
context creation.

Requirements:

1. When a new SUITE configuration context is
   created, load its local XML suite parameters.

2. Use the existing FrameworkParameterLayerLoader.

3. Register the values as a FRAMEWORK_PARAMETERS
   layer belonging to that SUITE context.

4. Apply the layer before the context is resolved
   and used by lifecycle callbacks.

5. Preserve existing source priority, including
   PROGRAMMATIC overrides taking precedence
   over FRAMEWORK_PARAMETERS.

6. Ensure context creation and parameter loading
   are atomic from the perspective of other threads.

7. Do not reload or overwrite the layer when
   an existing SUITE context is retrieved.

8. Preserve correct inheritance and lifecycle
   cleanup.

9. Do not implement TEST, CLASS or METHOD loading yet.

10. Do not modify the resolver, legacy properties
    manager or existing listeners.

Add one focused real TestNG integration test
verifying that:

- A suite XML property becomes available in the
  SUITE context.
- Two parallel XML test elements inherit it.
- An existing programmatic override retains
  its defined priority.
- No duplicate layers are registered.
- Cleanup removes the suite parameter layer.

Run the focused tests and report the result.

Keep the production change minimal.








